T.append(L(P+"t07","Transaction Management","high",
"Transaction management in Hibernate groups database operations into an atomic unit using Transaction begin, commit and rollback to maintain ACID properties.",
"Transaction me kai operations ek unit ki tarah hote hain: ya sab commit, ya koi error aaye to rollback. Hibernate me session.beginTransaction(), commit(), rollback().",
"Bank transfer: both debit and credit must succeed together or neither should happen.",
"Debit account A and credit account B inside one transaction; if the credit throws an exception, rollback restores A.",
["ACID: Atomicity, Consistency, Isolation, Durability.","Session.beginTransaction() → Transaction.commit()/rollback().","Pattern: try { … commit } catch { rollback } finally { close }.","Local (resource-local) vs JTA (container) transactions.","Isolation levels: read uncommitted, read committed, repeatable read, serializable.","Reads also need a transaction for consistency; one transaction per unit of work."],
["ACID.","Commit/rollback pattern.","Isolation levels."],
["Write transaction code.","Explain ACID.","Pick isolation level."],
["Not rolling back on exception.","Leaving transactions open."],
[E("explain with example","Write Hibernate code with commit and rollback.","try/catch pattern."),
 E("conceptual","Explain ACID.","Atomicity, Consistency, Isolation, Durability with bank example.")],
[Q("MCQ","Undo changes:","rollback()","",["commit()","rollback()","flush()","evict()"]),
 Q("true/false","commit makes changes permanent.","True",""),
 Q("short answer","Expand ACID.","Atomicity, Consistency, Isolation, Durability.",""),
 Q("scenario","Exception after first update. Action?","rollback the transaction",""),
 Q("comparison","JTA vs local transaction.","JTA is container-managed across resources; local is per connection.","")],
"Transactions: begin → commit / rollback; ACID; try-catch-finally; JTA vs local.",
syntax="Transaction tx = session.beginTransaction(); … tx.commit();",
code="Session s = sf.openSession();\nTransaction tx = null;\ntry {\n  tx = s.beginTransaction();\n  s.persist(new Student(1, \"Asha\"));\n  tx.commit();\n} catch (Exception e) {\n  if (tx != null) tx.rollback();\n  e.printStackTrace();\n} finally { s.close(); }",
expectedOutput="Committed on success; rollback and stack trace on failure",
codeExplanation="Rollback in catch prevents partial changes; finally always closes the session.",
apis=["Transaction.begin/commit/rollback","Session.beginTransaction","isolation levels"],
commonErrors=["TransactionRequiredException: no active transaction.","Forgetting finally close()."]))
